  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The OAI Provider handle the from and until arguments wrong.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We've tried to use the from and until parameters with the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "ListRecords verb.  The behaviour now seems to filter objects on",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "CreationDate and not LastModificationDate as expected.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The Filtering is done in the getDatePart method in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FedoraOAIProvider.java in line 340, where the FieldSearchQuery is",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "built. The query uses dcmDate instead of mDate, which is why it",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "filters on creationDate. If the dcmDate in the from and until",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "part are substituted mDate the FedoraOAIProvider works as",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "expected.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A patch file solving the problem is attached",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
